{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>From a month old and upward.</b> Once he is past the category of stillborns he is counted to be called a keeper of the charge of the sanctuary. Rabbi Yehuda bar Rabbi Shalom said: that tribe is practiced to be counted from the womb, as it is said ״אֲשֶׁר יָלְדָה אֹתָהּ לְלֵוִי בְּמִצְרָיִם״ (Numbers 26:59) — upon her entry at the threshold of Egypt she bore her, and she was counted among the seventy souls; for when you reckon their tally you find them only seventy less one, and she completed the count (Tanḥuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:13.812050194Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}